    "freeTraits": 0,
    "biography": "<h2>Background</h2><p>Born in Berlin during the last days of the First World War, Dieter Kotlar rose through the Nazi Party's ranks as a street enforcer before being Embraced in 1931 by the Brujah Isabella Correlli. He served the Third Reich as a member of the Death's Head Order through the Second World War, and returned to Berlin after Germany's defeat vowing to keep the ideals of the Reich alive. He now leads the Final Reich (also called the Fourth Reich), an anarch group nominally devoted to Nazi ideology that is, in truth, a tool Heinrich Himmler uses to expand Sabbat influence in Berlin and across Europe &mdash; a manipulation Dieter is equally happy to turn back on Himmler. In hand-to-hand combat, Dieter can flush his body with blood (at a cost of one Blood Point per turn) to deal aggravated wounds and inflict debilitating pain on his targets.</p><h2>Roleplaying Hints</h2><p>Smile and wave at anyone who looks your way, and slip in a line of propaganda whenever you can. You know the Final Reich holds the truth about how the world should be, and you're quick to anger if anyone mocks it. Deadly with insults, deadlier with fists &mdash; don't walk, swagger.</p>",
    "notes": "Haven: scattered locations across West and East Berlin, mostly poorly kept buildings. Publicly supports Gustav Breidenstein's claim to a unified Berlin. Secretly manipulated by his own sire's childe, Heinrich Himmler, into serving Sabbat interests. Lover of Erika Geiger, his own childe.",
    "npcType": "vampire"
  },
